WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.411 --> 00:00:02.744
(whooshing)

00:00:15.103 --> 00:00:17.341
- [Narrator] "Faith is
taking the first step

00:00:17.341 --> 00:00:20.443
"even when you don't see
the whole staircase."

00:00:20.443 --> 00:00:22.360
Martin Luther King, Jr.

00:00:23.351 --> 00:00:25.717
On August 23rd, 1963,
(inspirational music)

00:00:25.717 --> 00:00:28.672
a quarter of a million people
went to Washington D.C.

00:00:28.672 --> 00:00:30.934
to hear Martin Luther King, Jr.

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:33.071
speak at the Lincoln Memorial.

00:00:33.071 --> 00:00:35.925
How did he get so many people to come out?

00:00:35.925 --> 00:00:38.496
He didn't have a newsletter
or a Twitter account,

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:39.824
he wasn't making YouTube videos

00:00:39.824 --> 00:00:42.706
or using Google AdWords,
he didn't have a website

00:00:42.706 --> 00:00:44.103
or use Facebook.

00:00:44.103 --> 00:00:45.555
He didn't have any of the tools

00:00:45.555 --> 00:00:48.052
that make it so easy for us today

00:00:48.052 --> 00:00:50.661
to reach people and start movements,

00:00:50.661 --> 00:00:53.328
and yet 250,000 people came out.

00:00:54.761 --> 00:00:55.989
Why?

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:58.773
Because he stood for something important.

00:00:58.773 --> 00:01:01.457
The cause he believed in
touched people's hearts

00:01:01.457 --> 00:01:03.651
and led them to action.

00:01:03.651 --> 00:01:05.762
It was so important that people willingly

00:01:05.762 --> 00:01:08.637
spread the word and promoted his cause

00:01:08.637 --> 00:01:11.262
because it was their cause.

00:01:11.262 --> 00:01:13.699
You need to do the same.

00:01:13.699 --> 00:01:15.772
What does this have to do with business?

00:01:15.772 --> 00:01:17.896
You might be thinking, "That's great,

00:01:17.896 --> 00:01:19.934
"it works in political
or cultural movements,

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:22.664
"but what does it have
to do with business?"

00:01:22.664 --> 00:01:24.655
I'm glad you asked.

00:01:24.655 --> 00:01:26.914
What we're talking about
here is getting people

00:01:26.914 --> 00:01:29.935
to take action,
influencing decision making

00:01:29.935 --> 00:01:31.397
by appealing to something that people

00:01:31.397 --> 00:01:33.590
feel passionate about.

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.432
It can apply to going to your website

00:01:35.432 --> 00:01:37.992
and buying your product
just as easily as it does

00:01:37.992 --> 00:01:39.893
to getting in a bus and traveling to hear

00:01:39.893 --> 00:01:42.434
Martin Luther King, Jr. speak.

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:45.101
Most companies just never do it.

00:01:46.145 --> 00:01:47.551
Your business is not just about

00:01:47.551 --> 00:01:49.515
making a product or service.

00:01:49.515 --> 00:01:51.423
That's a recipe for failure.

00:01:51.423 --> 00:01:53.620
People want to know who you are

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:55.380
and what you stand for before they'll

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.717
buy anything from you.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.735
It's about standing
for something important

00:01:59.735 --> 00:02:03.652
and having your cause be
your customer's cause.

00:02:07.462 --> 00:02:09.795
(whooshing)

